  "enhanced_information": "In high performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) with gradient elution, the composition of the mobile phase varies throughout the chromatography process, allowing for the separation of complex mixtures as different compounds elute at different times. While temperature can be adjusted to optimize separation, it is not a defining characteristic of gradient elution. The pressure of the mobile phase is typically constant during a run, although it can be adjusted for flow rate. Therefore, the correct interpretation is that the composition of the mobile phase changes, while temperature and pressure are generally kept constant during the gradient elution process."
